  "root_cause": [
    "Ghidra confirms input_agent uses zte_fops; misc_register registers the miscdevice embedded at tcm+0x4a0, while syna_open converts that pointer back to tcm.",
    "The stock poll callback registers epoll waiters on tcm+0x448. Those waitqueue entries can outlive an individual poll call, while remove frees the tcm.",
    "The stock mmap callback maps the buffer at tcm+0x460; remove previously kfree’d that buffer even if a VMA remained.",
    "The exact probe registers input_agent before connect; connect failure and cdev-create failure did not reliably deregister the miscdevice."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Route input_agent open, poll, ioctl, mmap and release through generation-checked wrappers with active-operation references; reject stale opens and callbacks after quiesce.",
    "Deregister input_agent on connect failure, cdev-create failure and teardown.",
    "Retain the kmalloc mapping buffer through a per-open owner reference. Linux VMA file references keep the file context until its mappings are closed; final file release frees the retired buffer.",
    "Use a module-lifetime poll waitqueue so epoll registrations never point into the freed tcm. The wrapper around the preserved exact touch-report handler wakes the global queue after report publication; quiesce wakes it to deliver HUP/ERR.",
    "Wake both the stock ioctl frame waitqueue and the cdev waitqueue during quiesce; make the blocking input_agent ioctl return -ENODEV after shutdown."
  ],
